#==============================================================================================
#
#   environments_1 - HTML::Environment and HTML::EnvironmentSettingsObject; running script
#
#   DESCRIPTION:
#       Port of Libraries/LibWeb/HTML/Scripting/Environments.cpp (lines 37-285): the
#       environment and the environment settings object (construction, finalize, initialize,
#       visit_edges, discarding, the worker agents kept alive while starting, the realm
#       execution context, realm, global object, universal global scope and responsible event
#       loop), checking whether script can run, preparing to run and cleaning up after running
#       script and callbacks, the topmost script-having execution context, and parsing URLs
#       relative to an environment. The settings object registers with its responsible event
#       loop so that microtask checkpoints notify its global object about rejected promises.
